\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The observation operator \ensuremath  {\mathcal  {H}}\ maps the model field to the data vector \ensuremath  {\boldsymbol  {d}}\ in two steps: spatial interpolation to street-level sensors (a) and temporal averaging over intervals (b). Averaging suppresses the turbulent fluctuations so that ES-MDA\ targets the mean forcing. \textcolor {red}{[TODO: state $\ensuremath  {N_{d}}$, sensor count, interval length, and window relation.]}\relax }}{14}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:obs_operator}{{4}{14}{The observation operator \Hobs \ maps the model field to the data vector \obs \ in two steps: spatial interpolation to street-level sensors (a) and temporal averaging over intervals (b). Averaging suppresses the turbulent fluctuations so that \esmda \ targets the mean forcing. \todo {state $\Nd $, sensor count, interval length, and window relation.}\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Cross-model experimental design. A \emph  {truth model}\ (orange, top) generates synthetic observations $\ensuremath  {\boldsymbol  {d}}$ that are corrupted with noise and fed to ES-MDA; the \emph  {assimilation model}\ (teal, bottom) is a \emph  {different} solver and never sees the data-generating model, so its structural model discrepancy\ is real and irreducible. This is the setup that avoids the inverse crime\ of same-model twin experiment{s}. \textcolor {red}{[TODO: confirm ensemble size and window count shown.]}\relax }}{14}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cross_model_setup}{{5}{14}{Cross-model experimental design. A \truthmodel \ (orange, top) generates synthetic observations $\obs $ that are corrupted with noise and fed to \esmda ; the \assimmodel \ (teal, bottom) is a \emph {different} solver and never sees the data-generating model, so its structural \discrepancy \ is real and irreducible. This is the setup that avoids the \invcrime \ of same-model \twinexp {s}. \todo {confirm ensemble size and window count shown.}\relax }{figure.caption.7}{}}
